{
  "about": "A project's function files, codelist files and locks, read and admitted as a check reads them (FUNC-2, FILE-11, SCHEMA-2, CT-12), each case through both the check of the request's paths and the check of names relative to the study directory, which report the same rows. Moved at 8e662c648 from declaration_project_files.rs, whose tests read the same files through the public preparation or through a resolver that served them beside the project file, from project_environment.rs and project_diagnostics.rs, whose resolvers served held copies, and from file_project.rs. Most cases stage declaration_project_files.rs's study: the project lists one function file, holds a lock for each host and lists one codelist file, beside the specification's entry directory. The converted cases stage the 1.0 interface's adam-adsl-bmi example, its function file, its specification and the benchmark's R lock, which its tests read from the repository; the inline-codelist case stages project_environment.rs's listing, whose function file and lock it never reads. Each file is named by its path in the study.",
  "documents": {
    "project": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: project\nfunctions: [functions/id.yaml]\nenvironments:\n  python: {lock: uv.lock}\n  r: {lock: renv.lock}\ncodelists: [ct.yaml]\n",
    "id": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: function\nname: id\ndescription: Integer identity.\nparams: [{name: x, type: int, accepts_missing: true}]\nreturns: int\nmay_return_missing: true\nimplementations: {python: program.id, r: program::id}\ntests:\n  - {id: normal, covers: [normal, boundary], args: {x: 7}, result: 7}\n  - {id: missing, covers: ['accepted-missing:x', nullable-output], args: {x: null}, result: null}\n",
    "uv.lock": "version = 1\npackage = []\n",
    "renv.lock": "{\"R\": {\"Version\": \"4.6.1\"}, \"Packages\": {}}\n",
    "codelists": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: codelists\ncodelists: [{id: SEX, name: Sex, items: [{value: F}, {value: M}]}]\n",
    "domain": "yamaa: '1.0'\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\ninput: {SRC: {path: input.csv, types: {ID: int}}}\nkeys: [ID]\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: int, derivation: {function: {name: id, args: {x: SRC.ID}}}}\noutput: {path: output.csv, columns: [ID, VALUE]}\n",
    "sdtm": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: codelists\nstandard: {name: CDISC/NCI, publishing_set: SDTM, version: '2024-03-29'}\ncodelists:\n  - id: SEX\n    name: Sex\n    alias: C66731\n    format_name: $SEX\n    items:\n      - {value: F, decode: Female, alias: C16576}\n      - {value: M, decode: Male, alias: C20197}\n  - id: AGEGR\n    name: Age Group\n    data_type: integer\n    items: [{value: 1, decode: Young, rank: 1}, {value: 2, decode: Old, rank: 2}]\n  - id: MEDDRA\n    name: Adverse Event Dictionary\n    external: {dictionary: MedDRA, version: '26.0'}\n",
    "listing": "yamaa: '1.0'\ntype: project\nfunctions: [function.yaml]\nenvironments: {python: {lock: uv.lock}}\n"
  },
  "cases": [
    {
